# Left UNSET on purpose.
#
# With no value here, lib/api.ts derives the backend from the Expo dev server's
# own hostUri -- i.e. whatever LAN address this laptop has right now. Scan the
# QR on any network and it finds the backend, with nothing to edit.
#
# It used to pin an ngrok tunnel. ngrok free issues a NEW random URL every
# restart, so the moment that tunnel died every request from the app failed --
# login, alerts and the password reset alike. The reset looked especially
# broken because its endpoint returns success whether or not it worked, to
# avoid leaking which emails have accounts.
#
# Set this ONLY when the phone cannot reach the laptop directly -- mobile data,
# or a campus network that blocks client-to-client traffic. Then run
# `npm run start:tunnel` and paste the tunnel URL here.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://<something>.ngrok-free.dev/api
